## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates knowledge of edge ML deployment, covering model optimization, over-the-air updates, and monitoring strategies for resource-constrained environments.

## Key Concepts
- Edge inference using SageMaker Edge Manager
- Model quantization (INT8) for ARM64 architecture
- OTA updates via AWS IoT Jobs with rollback slots
- Local telemetry and validation with intermittent connectivity

## Code Example
```javascript
// Model inference with latency tracking
const model = loadModel('arm_int8.tflite');
const t0 = performance.now();
const output = model.run(input);
const latency = performance.now() - t0;

// Emit telemetry for edge agent
emitTelemetry({ latency, outputQuality: evaluateQuality(output) });
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant orchestration, real-time streaming inference, private isolation via PrivateLink, and drift-aware canaries across tenants.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Model Registry and Pipelines for per-tenant versioning
- PrivateLink and VPC isolation
- Per-tenant feature gating and rate limiting
- Drift detection using per-tenant feature distributions (Feature Store) and latency metrics
- Canary rollout governance with automatic rollback
- Cost modeling per tenant and region

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing and canary logic per tenant
function chooseModelForTenant(tenantId, payload) {
  const meta = loadTenantMeta(tenantId);
  const useCandidate = meta.canaryActive && Math.random() < meta.canaryTraffic;
  const model = useCandidate ? meta.candidateModel : meta.currentModel;
  return model.predict(payload);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant isolation in a shared endpoint?
- How would you monitor drift with streaming data?
- How do you escalate or rollback a tenant canary automatically when SLA is breached?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses design for multi-tenant ML services with strict data residency, private networking, and production-grade reliability, including canarying, drift handling, and cost accounting.

## Key Concepts

- PrivateLink and VPC isolation
- Multi-tenant routing architectures (per-tenant vs shared endpoint)
- Canary deployments with automatic rollback on drift/latency
- SageMaker Model Monitor for drift and quality checks
- KMS encryption and data residency controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-routing logic (illustrative only)
function routeRequest(tenantId, payload) {
  const endpoint = selectEndpointForTenant(tenantId);
  return invokeSageMaker(endpoint, payload);
}

function selectEndpointForTenant(tenantId) {
  // tenants mapped to endpoints or routing keys
  const map = {
    't1': 'endpoint-arn-1',
    't2': 'endpoint-arn-2'
  };
  return map[tenantId] || 'shared-endpoint-arn';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you design per-tenant quotas and rate limiting to prevent tail latency spikes?
- What metrics and alerting would you configure to detect drift early and trigger rollback?
